  "discussion": {
    "headline": "Sunny, dry and tranquil first week of meteorological summer",
    "dateLine": "11:30 a.m. Tuesday, June 2, 2026",
    "excerpt": "May ended on a sunny and beautiful note Sunday with high temperatures in the mid-to-upper 70s across the Lower Susquehanna Valley. However, the month was nothing short of volatile in terms of massive temperature swings. The season's first heatwave occurred from May 18-20 with a new record high of 96°F set at Millersville University on May 18. Just five days later, a wind-driven, soaking rain accompanied temperatures in the low 50s on the Saturday of Memorial Day Weekend. …",
    "url": "https://www.millersville.edu/weathercenter/forecasts/weather-discussion.php"
